## Nail Colors for Indian and South Asian Skin Tones: Wheatish to Deep

Wheatish to deep South Asian skin spans warm-medium to deep-warm, and the shade logic that works follows undertone the same way it does for every other tone in this guide, the range is simply wide and frequently underserved by mainstream content.

For wheatish skin with a warm undertone, which is common across this range, the strongest performers are warm nudes with a golden base, terracotta, deep coral, and a warm-toned maroon. These shades sit close enough to the skin's own warmth to look cohesive while still reading as a deliberate colour choice rather than camouflage.

For deeper South Asian skin tones, jewel-toned greens and a deep wine red both perform exceptionally well, particularly in a crème finish that lets the saturation carry the look without competing reflections. Gold-toned metallics also work across this entire range, from wheatish to deep, because the warmth of the metal complements the warmth typically present in the undertone.

The recurring complaint from South Asian readers, that nude polish "looks ashy" or "doesn't show up," almost always traces back to a nude that was developed for a cooler, paler undertone being applied to a warmer, deeper one. The fix is not a different depth of nude, it is a nude with a warmer base.

