## How to Test a Nail Colour Before You Commit

The test takes thirty seconds and it should be non-negotiable before any full manicure. Ask the technician to swatch the colour directly on your nail, not on a tip, not on a wheel held near your hand, on your actual nail bed.

The reason this matters is that nail beds carry their own pigment, separate from the surrounding skin, and that pigment interacts with translucent or sheer formulas in particular. A colour that looks one way on a plastic swatch can look noticeably different once it sits against your actual nail bed and the skin around it under the same light.

Natural light is part of the test too. Salon lighting is often warm and yellow-toned, which can flatter almost any colour in the moment and then look completely different the next morning by a window. If you can, step toward a window or door with the swatch on before deciding. If you are also deciding on shape alongside colour, <a href="/blog/almond-nail-colors-skin-tone">almond nail colours for every skin tone</a> maps colour recommendations to the almond shape specifically, which is worth a look before your next appointment.

