## 2026 Trending Colours Mapped to Your Skin Tone

Butter yellow was everywhere at the start of the year, and on a huge number of hands, it simply did not work. The shade itself was not the problem, the undertone mismatch was. Butter yellow leans heavily warm and low-saturation, which means it can wash out cool undertones almost completely while reading as soft and flattering on warm ones, a perfect case study for why a trending colour is only worth adopting once you know your undertone can carry it.

2026's other major movements, deep cherry reds, warm earthy neutrals, and unexpected metallic accents, all follow the same pattern. Cherry red leans cool enough to suit cool and neutral undertones across almost every depth, while the warm earthy neutrals (think clay, fawn, and toasted caramel) sit naturally with warm undertones from fair through deep. Metallic accents, particularly in copper and rose-gold tones, have shown up across medium and deep skin tones as a way to add interest without committing to a full bold colour.

